WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.180
This is the Microsoft for Education Daily, for Sunday.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.270
Here are the last 24 hours at Microsoft, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.280
Everyone in. The week's best: for Windows Insiders,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.240
Narrator now shows math on a Braille display.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.500
Students who read Braille can explore equations by touch,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.060
in Word, PowerPoint, Edge or Chrome.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.530
Chatting in class? Insiders' Live captions can now follow your mic,

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.340
your PC's sound, or both.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.000
Over in Copilot Chat, App Blocks are rolling out: ask,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.560
and get a working calculator, planner or simulation.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.360
Picture a practice form, or a simple physics simulation,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.170
built right inside the chat.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.610
Signing in? Insiders' Windows Hello now takes face,

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.670
fingerprint or PIN, whichever works first.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.490
Campus IT? In Teams,

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:07.230
tagging @GitHub is now generally available: from bug report to pull request.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.180
Its new Canvas puts the plan,

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.770
the code changes and a preview right beside the conversation.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.330
In Entra, Conditional Access policy plans are in preview: define who's covered once,

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.340
then add rules.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.910
And for IT, Insiders' Windows Hello now logs which method people used,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.240
and failed sign-ins.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.420
Student coders? Microsoft's Pro Badge for GitHub Copilot is free,

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:37.480
with no exam: it's earned from everyday use.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.820
Opt in with a personal GitHub account,

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.920
reach Proficient, and the badge is yours to share.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.670
The fine print? .NET 8 and 9 reach end of support on Tuesday, November 10.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.190
And two shared screens side by side in Teams Rooms?

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.660
Now due in January, not December.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.690
After hours?

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:07.520
About 80% of The End of the Sun's objects were scanned from real ones.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:10.900
Spot something unfamiliar?

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.300
Optional Learn More points tell you what it was used for.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.300
And on Xbox, EA Play now has Plants vs. Zombies: Replanted,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.430
with local co-op, and MySims: Cozy Bundle.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.880
Math by touch, captions for the room,

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.230
apps in the chat: the week's best gets everyone in.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.020
Day after day, the updates keep stacking up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.340
Today's board: shipped. Tomorrow's: already building.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
That's one day of updates. Imagine a whole year.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.720
This has been the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?
